<statement>
<p>
Fill in the missing pieces in the conversion of the decimal integer <m>\displaystyle{\left({22}\right)}_{{{10}}}</m> into its binary (base-2) representation.
</p>
<p>
22 = 2<asterisk/>(<fillin characters="1" />) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
11 = 2<asterisk/>(<fillin characters="1" />) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
5 = 2<asterisk/>(<fillin characters="1" />) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
2 = 2<asterisk/>(<fillin characters="1" />) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
1 = 2<asterisk/>(<fillin characters="1" />) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
The binary representation of <m>\displaystyle{\left({22}\right)}_{{{10}}}</m> is <m>\displaystyle{(}</m><fillin characters="1" /><m>\displaystyle{)}_{{{2}}}</m>.

</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p><ul><li>11</li><li>0</li><li>5</li><li>1</li><li>2</li><li>1</li><li>1</li><li>0</li><li>0</li><li>1</li><li>10110</li></ul></p>
</solution>
